WEBVTT

00:00.620 --> 00:03.210
The following graph represents
the first five terms

00:03.210 --> 00:04.499
of two given patterns.

00:04.499 --> 00:06.540
In the answer box, there
are different statements

00:06.540 --> 00:07.498
about the two patterns.

00:07.498 --> 00:09.320
Choose all correct statements.

00:09.320 --> 00:11.700
So here, for each point,
this point right over here,

00:11.700 --> 00:13.750
this represents its
horizontal coordinate

00:13.750 --> 00:16.086
is the first term of
pattern A, which is 4.

00:16.086 --> 00:17.960
And its vertical coordinate
is the first term

00:17.960 --> 00:19.149
in pattern B, which is 1.

00:19.149 --> 00:21.440
And then we could do that
for the other points as well.

00:21.440 --> 00:23.990
So actually, let's figure
out what the values are.

00:23.990 --> 00:29.160
So we have pattern A and
then we have pattern B.

00:29.160 --> 00:32.680
So the first term
for pattern A is 4.

00:32.680 --> 00:38.590
And when pattern A is 4, the
first term for pattern B is 1.

00:38.590 --> 00:42.330
The second term
for pattern A is 7.

00:42.330 --> 00:46.680
And when pattern A is
7, pattern B is also 7.

00:46.680 --> 00:53.080
Third term, pattern A is
10, and pattern B is 13.

00:53.080 --> 00:59.590
And then the fourth
term, pattern A is 13,

00:59.590 --> 01:03.130
and pattern B is 19.

01:03.130 --> 01:08.910
And then finally, fifth
term, pattern A is 16,

01:08.910 --> 01:14.534
and pattern B is 25.

01:14.534 --> 01:15.950
Now, before even
looking at these,

01:15.950 --> 01:18.700
let's see what we can think
about these patterns here.

01:18.700 --> 01:21.070
So it looks like
pattern A starts at 4,

01:21.070 --> 01:24.320
and it increases
by 3 every time.

01:24.320 --> 01:29.490
To go from one term to the
next, you just have to add 3.

01:29.490 --> 01:32.160
Now, what about for pattern B?

01:32.160 --> 01:35.170
Well pattern B starts at
1, and every term here it

01:35.170 --> 01:36.550
looks like you're adding 6.

01:36.550 --> 01:39.050
So when pattern A
increases by 3 and we're

01:39.050 --> 01:42.155
moving in the horizontal
direction based on the fact

01:42.155 --> 01:45.270
that pattern A is represented
on the horizontal axis,

01:45.270 --> 01:47.490
we're going to move up
6 in the vertical axis,

01:47.490 --> 01:48.460
and we see that here.

01:52.000 --> 01:55.230
Pattern A increases by 3
from one term to the next.

01:55.230 --> 01:57.220
And when that increased
by 3, pattern B

01:57.220 --> 01:59.820
increased by 6 from
one term to the next.

02:03.740 --> 02:09.680
And we see that it
keeps doing that.

02:09.680 --> 02:12.160
Now, let's think about
what we have over here

02:12.160 --> 02:16.100
to see which of these statements
actually apply to this.

02:16.100 --> 02:18.900
For every term in pattern
A, multiply the term by 2

02:18.900 --> 02:21.640
and then subtract 7 to get the
corresponding term from pattern

02:21.640 --> 02:24.690
B. So let's see
if that holds up.

02:24.690 --> 02:26.780
So according to this,
if this was true,

02:26.780 --> 02:28.910
I should be able to take
this, multiply it by 2

02:28.910 --> 02:30.990
and subtract 7 and get that.

02:30.990 --> 02:31.580
So let's see.

02:31.580 --> 02:37.380
Is 1 equal to 2 times 8 minus 7?

02:37.380 --> 02:39.490
Sorry, 2 times 4 minus 7.

02:39.490 --> 02:43.090
So 2 times this number,
2 times 4 minus 7.

02:43.090 --> 02:45.610
Well, 8 minus 7 is equal to 1.

02:45.610 --> 02:51.660
Is this right over here equal
to 2 times this 7 minus 7?

02:51.660 --> 02:53.510
Well, yeah, it's equal to 7.

02:53.510 --> 02:59.594
Is 13 equal to 2
times 10 minus 7?

02:59.594 --> 03:02.130
Well, yeah, 20 minus 7 is 13.

03:02.130 --> 03:06.870
Is 19 equal to 2
times 13 minus 7?

03:06.870 --> 03:09.210
26 minus 7 is 19.

03:09.210 --> 03:13.400
Is 25 equal to 2
times 16 minus 7?

03:13.400 --> 03:17.060
Well, 32 minus 7 is 25.

03:17.060 --> 03:20.360
So this first
statement checks out.

03:20.360 --> 03:24.880
For the corresponding term,
the value of pattern B

03:24.880 --> 03:29.475
is two times the value
of pattern A minus 7.

03:29.475 --> 03:30.850
Now let's look at
the second one.

03:30.850 --> 03:32.370
The terms of
pattern B are always

03:32.370 --> 03:34.470
greater than or equal to
their corresponding terms

03:34.470 --> 03:37.630
from pattern A. Well,
no, that's not right.

03:37.630 --> 03:39.130
It's true for a
couple of scenarios.

03:39.130 --> 03:41.380
Here for the third,
fourth, and fifth term,

03:41.380 --> 03:45.670
or actually for the second,
third, fourth, and fifth terms,

03:45.670 --> 03:47.977
pattern B is equal to or
greater than pattern A.

03:47.977 --> 03:49.560
But for the first
term, it's not true.

03:49.560 --> 03:53.520
Pattern A is greater,
so this is not right.

03:53.520 --> 03:55.190
To get from each
point to the next,

03:55.190 --> 03:58.080
you need to move 3 units to
the right and 6 units up.

03:58.080 --> 03:59.830
Well, that's exactly
what we talked about.

03:59.830 --> 04:01.550
From one term to
the next, pattern A,

04:01.550 --> 04:04.710
along our horizontal
axis, we increased by 3,

04:04.710 --> 04:08.620
while pattern B, which is
plotted on our vertical axis,

04:08.620 --> 04:09.620
by 6.

04:09.620 --> 04:12.580
So you move 3 to
the right and 6 up.

04:12.580 --> 04:14.630
So that is right.

04:14.630 --> 04:16.874
The second terms of
both patterns are 7.

04:16.874 --> 04:18.540
Well, yeah, we see
that right over here.

04:18.540 --> 04:19.950
The second terms are 7.

04:19.950 --> 04:24.770
We have 7 here, and
we have 7 there.

04:24.770 --> 04:26.090
And so that is right as well.

04:26.090 --> 04:28.730
So the only one that doesn't
apply is this second one.

04:28.730 --> 04:30.970
This is not right.
